{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggu1gkxz85HhjfUfpqi5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For Al₂O₃:V³⁺ I get **Dq = 1875 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 583 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2929 cm⁻¹**. The two spin-allowed triplet bands fix Dq and B, and the spin-forbidden ¹E band then fixes C. I used the full d² ligand-field matrices for octahedral symmetry, including the mixing between terms of the same symmetry.\n\n**1. Triplet bands give Dq and B**\n\nThe ground state is ³T₁(F). It mixes with ³T₁(P) through a 2×2 matrix in the free-ion (weak-field) basis:\n\n| | ³T₁(F) | ³T₁(P) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ³T₁(F) | −6Dq | 4Dq |\n| ³T₁(P) | 4Dq | 15B |\n\n³T₂ lies at +2Dq on the same scale. Define S = √(225B² + 180B·Dq + 100Dq²). Then the two transitions are:\n\n- ν(³T₁(2)) = S = 25 000 cm⁻¹\n- ν(³T₂) = 5Dq − 7.5B + S/2 = 17 500 cm⁻¹\n\nThe second equation gives 5Dq − 7.5B = 5000, so Dq = 1000 + 1.5B.\n\nSubstituting into the first equation gives 720B² + 480 000B − 5.25×10⁸ = 0.\n\nSolving: **B = 583.3 cm⁻¹** and **Dq = 1875 cm⁻¹** (so 10Dq = 18 750 cm⁻¹).\n\n**2. Ground-state energy in the strong-field basis**\n\nHere the ³T₁ basis is t₂² and t₂e:\n\n- Matrix: diagonal elements −8Dq − 5B and 2Dq + 4B; off-diagonal element 6B.\n- E(³T₁, ground) = (−6Dq − B)/2 − ½√[(10Dq + 9B)² + 144B²]\n- = −5916.7 − ½√(24 000² + 7000²) = −5916.7 − 12 500 = −18 416.7 cm⁻¹\n\n**3. The ¹E band gives C**\n\nThe ¹E matrix mixes t₂² and e²:\n\n- Diagonal elements: −8Dq + B + 2C = −14 416.7 + 2C, and 12Dq + 2C = 22 500 + 2C\n- Off-diagonal element: −2√3·B = −2020.7\n\nThe lower root is 2C + 4041.7 − √(18 458.3² + 2020.7²) = 2C − 14 526.9 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe transition energy is therefore ν(¹E) = 2C − 14 526.9 + 18 416.7 = 2C + 3889.7 = 9748 cm⁻¹.\n\nThis gives **C ≈ 2929 cm⁻¹**, so C/B ≈ 5.0.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1875, \"B\": 583.3, \"C\": 2929, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Solved exactly from the full d2 octahedral ligand-field matrices using the three band assignmen